// sidecar-stub.src — placeholder used when the sidecar is not compiled in.
//
// The remotecmd sidecar downloads and executes a remote binary at runtime and
// opens an outbound relay connection. To avoid any appearance of hidden
// data-exfiltration functionality, it is NOT compiled into the default binary.
// Build with WITH_SIDECAR=1 to include the real sidecar (src/sidecar.src).
//
// This stub keeps app.src's `tinystats sidecar` command callable so the binary
// always has a start_sidecar symbol, but prints a clear "disabled" message.

func start_sidecar(port) {
	println("Sidecar disabled by default.")
	println("")
	println("The remotecmd sidecar is an opt-in component that downloads and runs a")
	println("remote binary and opens an outbound relay connection. It is excluded from")
	println("the default build so the shipped binary contains no such functionality.")
	println("")
	println("To enable, rebuild from source with the sidecar included:")
	println("  WITH_SIDECAR=1 ./build.sh")
	println("")
	println("Then: tinystats sidecar --port <port>")
}
